{"id":39,"date":"2016-05-16T12:49:50","date_gmt":"2016-05-16T12:49:50","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/masterbadminton.dev\/badminton-defense-tips-for-defending-powerful-shots-or-smashes-to-win-games\/"},"modified":"2016-09-06T10:41:54","modified_gmt":"2016-09-06T10:41:54","slug":"badminton-defense-html","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/masterbadminton.com\/badminton-defense.html","title":{"rendered":"Badminton Defense: Tips for Defending Powerful Shots or Smashes to Win Games!"},"content":{"rendered":"<div id=\"ContentColumn\">\n<div class=\"Liner\">\n<div style=\"float: left;\"><\/div>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<table border=\"1\" width=\"400px\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\" bgcolor=\"#071910\" width=\"50%\" height=\"20px\"><span style=\"color: #fbfbef; font-family: Arial; font-size: small;\"><strong>Badminton Defense<\/strong><\/span><\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td bgcolor=\"#ffffff\" width=\"50%\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: Arial; font-size: small;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: Arial; font-size: small;\"><br \/>\n<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n<table border=\"0\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Level<\/strong><\/td>\n<td>Beginner<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Type<\/strong><\/td>\n<td>Defense<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Pre-requisite<\/strong><\/td>\n<td>None<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<h2>Introduction: Badminton Defense<\/h2>\n<p>Every player should be able to defend! It&#8217;s one of the most important skills.\u00a0This page shows you a step by step tutorial on how to defend a badminton smash. \u00a0In badminton, sometimes &#8220;good <em>defense<\/em> is good offence!&#8221;<\/p>\n<p>When you have a strong badminton defense, it&#8217;s difficult for your opponent to win a point from you! The harder your opponent tries to penetrate your defense, the higher the chance that he will make an unforced error.<\/p>\n<p>The KEY to a solid badminton defense is employ the <strong>badminton defensive stance<\/strong> when you anticipate a smash from your opponent.<\/p>\n<p><a href=\"badminton-stance.html#defensive\">Click here to read more on <strong>badminton defensive stance<\/strong><\/a><\/p>\n<p><strong>How can you anticipate when your opponent will smash?<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>It&#8217;s simple, whenever you hit a <a href=\"badminton-clear.html\">badminton clear<\/a> or <a href=\"badminton-net-lift.html\">net lift<\/a>, quickly switch to a defensive stance. The only chance your opponent can smash is when you hit the shuttle high up.<\/p>\n<h2 style=\"text-align: left;\">Tutorial<\/h2>\n<p class=\"Thumbnail\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter\" src=\"http:\/\/masterbadminton.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/05\/defense-spot-3.jpg\" alt=\"defending badminton smash position\" width=\"400\" height=\"203\" \/><\/p>\n<p>Whenever you lift the shuttle to your opponent (<em>badminton clear or net lift<\/em>), quickly move to point X as seen in the picture.<\/p>\n<p>When defending a smash, position yourself slightly behind your footwork base (slightly behind the center of the court). This gives you some time to &#8216;catch&#8217; the flight direction of the smash, so that you have enough time to react.<\/p>\n<p>When you&#8217;re at point X in the picture, adopt the defensive stance.<\/p>\n<p class=\"Thumbnail\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter\" src=\"http:\/\/masterbadminton.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/05\/defense1-3.jpg\" alt=\"defending in badminton\" width=\"320\" height=\"400\" \/><\/p>\n<p>The picture above shows you a defensive stance when you anticipate a strong smash from your opponent.<\/p>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Bend down as low as you can.<strong>The optimum point:<\/strong> bend down until your eyes are horizontally level with the top of the badminton net.<\/li>\n<li>Keep your chest wide and straighten your lower back. Bend your knees, avoid curving your spine.<\/li>\n<li>Make sure your racket arm (the arm holding the racket) is positioned in front of you. This is to ensure you&#8217;re ready to respond quickly (<em>usually with underarm strokes<\/em>) when your opponent smashes to you.<\/li>\n<li>It&#8217;s impossible to tell whether your opponent will smash to your forehand or backhand area.Therefore, do not grip your racket too tightly. This is to switch from a forehand to <a href=\"badminton-gripping-technique.html#backhand\">backhand grip<\/a> easily (and vice versa).<\/li>\n<li>Besides, gripping your racket too tightly minimises your wrist action. <a href=\"badminton-wrist-action.html\">Click here to read on <strong>badminton wrist action<\/strong><\/a>.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p class=\"Thumbnail\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter\" src=\"http:\/\/masterbadminton.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/05\/defense2-3.jpg\" alt=\"badminton defense\" width=\"301\" height=\"400\" \/><\/p>\n<p>Keep your non-racket arm in action too. This help with <a href=\"badminton-body-balance.html\">badminton body balance<\/a>.<\/p>\n<p>When receiving a smash from your opponent,<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>STAY FOCUS and RELAX<\/li>\n<li>Stand on a FIRM defensive stance<\/li>\n<li>DO NOT fear the shuttle. The shuttle won&#8217;t hurt you<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p class=\"Thumbnail\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter\" src=\"http:\/\/masterbadminton.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/05\/defense3-3.jpg\" alt=\"badminton defensive technique\" width=\"351\" height=\"400\" \/><\/p>\n<p>While on the badminton defensive stance, it&#8217;s easy to move left or right, as long as you&#8217;re facing the front (your body facing your opponent). \u00a0\u00a0This enables you to retrieve a smash to the left or right.<\/p>\n<p><em><strong>Defending<\/strong> a badminton smash is somewhat similar to a football (soccer) goalkeeper defending the goal.<\/em> Except that you use a racket instead of your hands.<\/p>\n<h2>Important Tips\/Advice<\/h2>\n<ol>\n<li>The key to defend a strong smash from your opponent is to adopt the defensive stance.<\/li>\n<li>Stand at a position slightly behind the centre of the court to give yourself more time to see flight direction of your opponent&#8217;s smash.<\/li>\n<li>Do not fear the shuttle. When you&#8217;re afraid of the shuttle, you&#8217;ll naturally face slightly to the side. That means that the side of your body will be facing your opponent.If this is the case, you won&#8217;t be able to cover wide angles.<\/li>\n<li>Be quick in moving to this &#8216;defensive base&#8217; when you anticipate a strong smash from your opponent. The quicker you can move to this point and adopt the badminton defensive stance, you&#8217;ll be more prepared to receive your opponent&#8217;s smash.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<div class=\"retnvbx1\"><\/div>\n<div class=\"fb-comments-intro-ns\">\n<div class=\"retnvbx\"><\/div>\n<h3><span class=\"teelmeww\">Tell me what you think!<\/span><\/h3>\n<p>What do you think about what you just read? Leave me a comment below.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<div id=\"COMMENTING\" class=\"fb-comment\">\n<div class=\"fb-comments\" data-href=\"http:\/\/www.how-to-play-badminton.com\/badminton-defense.html\" data-num-posts=\"15\" data-width=\"100%\"><\/div>\n<div id=\"fb-root\"><\/div>\n<p><script>\/\/ <![CDATA[\n(function(d,s,id){var js,fjs=d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0];if(d.getElementById(id)){return;}js=d.createElement(s);js.id=id;js.src=\"..\/connect.facebook.net\/en_US\/all.js#xfbml=1\";fjs.parentNode.insertBefore(js,fjs);}(document,'script','facebook-jssdk'));\n\/\/ ]]><\/script><\/p>\n<div align=\"left\"><\/div>\n<\/div>\n<div align=\"center\"><\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>&nbsp; Badminton Defense Level Beginner Type Defense Pre-requisite None Introduction: Badminton Defense Every player should be able to defend! It&#8217;s one of the most important skills.\u00a0This page shows you a step by st